# kin/youth/wear/dress: the youth girl's dress (the A3 woman's dress at 26 px): the bodice in cloth 1 with the waist a
# pixel in on each side, the chemise (linen) at the round neckline and the puff caps of the shoulders (the arms draw the
# puff sleeve: regionsOf's dress sets U linen, C skin), the apron's bib (cloth 3) over the belly; dress_hang carries the
# skirt and the apron to the ankles. A girl's garment: one fit (the A3 woman's), so no `when girl` replacements.
# KIN-YOUTH (P2b fix round 1: before it the youth had no dress, and rig 2 drew a girl in a dress with v1's whole sprite).
# (P2b motion rollout 2026-10-22, KIN-YOUTH) on the torso channel (keys torso): the side walk names `run` (the rest view),
# the run `runl` (rows 0-1 as rest, 2-3 a pixel back, 4 two back: under kin_youth.clip's lean 3 the chest leads the waist
# by 2 and the belt sits over hip 1); L `lie` repeats the rest view for the turned fall frames. The girl's run views carry
# the boy's belt row (and in the leaning run her waist row): the belt rides her hips, so her thighs start inside them.
# Every rest view is untouched.
use person woman
body youth
role garment dress
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso

